          "en": "The speaker describes examining many Shastras and Smritis, then says that they do not reach the value of Naam. The claim is not that literacy or careful study is forbidden: the salok itself speaks from examination. It concerns the limits of learned systems when compared with direct orientation towards the Divine. Amol means beyond a fixed price. The Ashtpadi develops this comparison by asking whether outward achievements actually remove ego and change conduct.",
