        "en": "Ashtpadi 9 examines religious identities through the qualities of life they should express. Aparas is opened through inner purity; Vaishnav through selfless devotion and compassion; bhagauti through love and service of Bhagvant; pandit through understanding and teaching that benefits all. Naam is accessible across the four varnas named in the passage. Ramdas is defined as the genuine servant of the Divine, and jivan mukti as liberation while alive in loving acceptance of Divine command. The final pauri gathers these states within the One who creates, gives understanding and remains compassionate.",
